[[File:Berserk manga vol. 1 (2016).png|thumb|Cover for the 2016 edition of volume 1, featuring [[Guts (Berserk)|Guts]]|alt=Illustration of Guts, an armored, muscular man, resting his hands on the hilt of his sword]]
''[[Berserk (manga)|Berserk]]'' is a Japanese [[manga]] series created by [[Kentaro Miura]], published by [[Hakusensha]] in the magazines ''Monthly Animal House'' (1989–1992) and ''[[Young Animal (magazine)|Young Animal]]'' (since 1992). Since the late 2000s, the manga has been published irregularly, with frequent hiatuses. Following Miura's death in 2021, the series has been continued and supervised by Miura's friend, [[Kouji Mori]], and drawn by Studio Gaga, consisting of Miura's assistants and apprentices.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2022-06-07/berserk-manga-continues-under-kentarou-miura-assistants-kouji-mori-supervision/.186405|title=Berserk Manga Continues Under Kentarou Miura's Assistants, Kouji Mori's Supervision|author=Pineda, Rafael Antonio|date=2022-06-07|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=2023-03-14|archive-date=June 7, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220607053508/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2022-06-07/berserk-manga-continues-under-kentarou-miura-assistants-kouji-mori-supervision/.186405|url-status=live}}</ref>

The story follows [[Guts (Berserk)|Guts]], an orphaned mercenary on his quest for revenge, and consists of five major [[story arc]]s: {{Nihongo foot|"The Black Swordsman Arc"|黒い剣士篇|Kuroi Kenshi-hen|group=nb}} (volumes 1–3); {{Nihongo foot|"Golden Age Arc"|黄金時代篇|Ōgon Jidai-hen|group=nb}} (volumes 3–14); {{Nihongo foot|"Conviction Arc"|断罪篇|Danzai-hen|group=nb}} (volumes 14–21); {{Nihongo foot|"Falcon of the Millennium Empire Arc"|{{ruby-ja|千年王国の鷹|ミレニアム・ファルコン}}編|Mireniamu Farukon-hen|{{lit|Millennium Falcon Arc}}|group=nb}} (volumes 22–35); and {{Nihongo foot|"Fantasia Arc"|{{ruby-ja|幻造世界|ファンタジア}}編|Fantajia-hen|group=nb}} (volumes 35–).<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:ストーリーチャート STORY CHART|url=https://www.berserk-project.jp/dictionary/storychart.html|website=berserk-project.jp|access-date=June 22, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180903013355/http://berserk-project.jp/dictionary/storychart.html|archive-date=September 3, 2018|language=ja|url-status=live}}</ref>

The chapters (called "episodes") are collected by Hakusensha in {{Transliteration|ja|[[tankōbon]]}} volumes, with the first volume released on November 26, 1990; the posthumous 41st volume, which includes the final chapters that Miura had created for the series, was released in 2021.<ref>{{cite web|last=Pineda|first=Rafael|title=Berserk Manga's 1st Volume in 3 Years Ships on December 24|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2021-09-05/berserk-manga-1st-volume-in-3-years-ships-on-december-24/.177044|website=[[Anime News Network]]|access-date=September 11, 2024|date=September 5, 2021|archive-date=September 6, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210906031005/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2021-09-05/berserk-manga-1st-volume-in-3-years-ships-on-december-24/.177044|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:「ベルセルク」41巻本日発売、ニューヨーク・タイムズ、ル・モンド、朝日新聞に広告掲載|url=https://natalie.mu/comic/news/459105|website=[[Comic Natalie]]|publisher=Natasha, Inc|access-date=September 11, 2024|language=ja|date=December 24, 2021|archive-date=December 23, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211223200109/https://natalie.mu/comic/news/459105|url-status=live}}</ref> 43 have been released as of 2025. [[Dark Horse Comics]] has been releasing the English editions of the volumes since October 22, 2003, and began publishing hardcover editions containing multiple volumes on February 27, 2019.<ref name="BerserkD-vol1"/> The Japanese volumes were re-released with new cover art starting in 2016, following the rebranding of Hakusensha's Jets Comics imprint as Young Animal Comics.<ref>{{cite web|script-title=ja:ジェッツコミックスが名称変更！「ベルセルク」38巻発売&全巻リニューアル|url=https://natalie.mu/comic/news/182748|website=[[Comic Natalie]]|publisher=Natasha, Inc|access-date=May 22, 2020|language=ja|date=April 8, 2016|archive-date=April 17, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210417032342/https://natalie.mu/comic/news/182748|url-status=live}}</ref>
